ampire, a Black Spiral Cub, a Bane Mummy, and a Qyrlling. They must discover how to destroy them and save the town.<br /> <br /> It: (MAINE! *takes a shot*) A group of friends must band together and banish a Earthbound before the Demon feasts again.<br /> <br /> My suggestions.<br /> <br /> Dracula, Frankenstein, The Mummy, The Invisible Man, The Wolf Man, Creature of the Black Lagoon, The Phantom of the Opera.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T23:30:48-08:00","id":412489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PaladinDemo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/401419-explain-a-movie-tv-show-comic-in-wod-terms?p=410930#post410930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It: (MAINE! *takes a shot*) A group of friends must band together and banish a Earthbound before the Demon feasts again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Incidentally, because of the age jump, I've always liked <b>IT</b> as a <i>Changeling</i> adventure.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Dracula </div> </div> </div>Well, the obvious choice is hunters (mundane or otherwise) going after a Tzimisce who has just moved to London. That gives you the ties to Eastern Europe, why Dracula would be importing dirt . . .<br /> <br /> <i>However,</i> you could also run <i>Dracula</i> as a situation of gruesome mistaken identity. Throughout the novel, Dracula <i>never</i> does &quot;supernatural&quot; stuff in front of third party witnesses. In fact, the only people who ever see any &quot;vampiric&quot; activity are Harker &amp; Co. Heck, Dracula even walks around London in broad daylight. And really, the whole novel reads like an inquest into why Harker <i>et al</i> felt the need to chase a Transylvanian expatriate across the continent before murdering him in his home. So you could see it as a cautionary tale for other hunters about getting too obsessed with a hunt, and missing clues that your target is just a mundane human<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Phantom of the Opera. </div> </div> </div>There's nothing explicitly supernatural about the Phantom, but you could do an interesting version where (instead of being injured), he's embraced by a Nosferatu to preserve his voice. That gives you the hideous appearance, living in the catacombs . . .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T09:52:49-08:00","id":412903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> 