/div> </div> </div>I think this one is probably truest to the original story. I think The Persian would be the Torrie ghoul, or the Kindred himself with Phillipe or Raoul as his ghoul.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T17:33:50-08:00","id":413458,"title":"","content":"ok, explain Jaws and Friday the 13th part one and two","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T21:18:19-08:00","id":413709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/401419-explain-a-movie-tv-show-comic-in-wod-terms?p=413458#post413458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Friday the 13th part one and two</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Part One:</b> Female mage - driven mad by grief over the loss of her son - devotes her life to raising him from the dead, pursuing all sorts of dark power. And then someone decides to reopen the summer camp where he died. In her madness, she can't distinguish the new camp counselors from the ones who let him drown, all those years ago . . . and decides that a little human sacrifice might be just the ticket . . .<br /> <br /> <b>Part Two:</b> Behold the fruits of her labor! Her dark experiments have created her own flawed version of a Bane Mummy. Turns out Jason didn't die of drowning - just suffered massive brain damage. He lived to be a large, shambling hulk of a man before dying of unknown causes (his mother's magic, perhaps? Or maybe outright murder, a desperate attempt to get away from being responsible for him?)<br /> <br /> But with his mother's death, the wards she place on her experiment collapse . . . and the variant Bane Mummy escapes. Still mentally damaged, and having absorbed a lifetime of hatred from her, the Bane Mummy seeks to murder the teens she hated so much. And his Ka - when manifest - appears as young teenage Jason (but only under water - remember, its a flawed experiment).<br /> <br /> And, of course, since he's a mummy (albeit a Bane one), there's no way to truly kill him. No matter how badly his body is damaged, or how many times he's &quot;killed&quot;, what's left of his soul will (eventually) be able to repair the damage and bring him back . . .<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T21:23:47-08:00","id":413713,"title":"","content":"Jason would be a Formori Gorehound, probably a prototype of one that can resurrect itself.<br /> <br /> Jaws: A Ixtal Rokea is terrorizing the New England shoreline. Devouring those who enter the water. While some were Wyrm tainted, others were not. The local Sheriff, a Marine Biologist, and a shark fisherman set out to slay the &quot;rogue&quot; shark.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":1442,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","user":"PaladinDemo","date":".  Jaws edit. 02-21-2015, 12:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-21T09:50:31-08:00","id":414113,"title":"","content":"ok..Explain Halloween ( 1970 's ), Tremors and The Lawnmower Man","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/175