er Things, an Amalgam of NWO and Progenitor Technocrats experiments on creating Enlightened children goes awry and results in their greatest success accidentally tearing a permanent hole in the Penumbra, unleashing the spawn of a powerful Bane Spirit on a small Midwestern town.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I get Void Engineers more than Progenitors from Stranger Things, but maybe that's just me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-17T20:52:26-08:00","id":1168471,"title":"","content":"Miss Kobayashi's Dragon Maid: Normal human plays host to a bunch of dragon Bygones (who take human form to dodge Disbelief), because the material world is a change of pace from the high fantasy Umbral Realm they usually inhabit. One of the human's neighbors is the young son of a Mage.<br /> <br /> (Honestly, that one was too easy.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-18T09:08:17-08:00","id":1168540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/401419-explain-a-movie-tv-show-comic-in-wod-terms?p=1168471#post1168471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Miss Kobayashi's Dragon Maid: Normal human plays host to a bunch of dragon Bygones (who take human form to dodge Disbelief), because the material world is a change of pace from the high fantasy Umbral Realm they usually inhabit. One of the human's neighbors is the young son of a Mage.<br /> <br /> (Honestly, that one was too easy.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Dragon Maid doesn't really follow a pattern of &quot;Bygones avoid disbelief&quot;, as the dragons don't interfere only because the powers in their own world would become upset if they went around wreaking utter havoc. They're none the worse for wear when they use their true powers, which they often do on a normal playground, in full view of others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-18T10:28:23-08:00","id":1168555,"title":"","content":"Blade Runner, a retired NWO operative is reactivated and hunts down a group of renegade Victors who are seeking a Master Progenitor to extend their lifespans. <br /> Tomorrowland, a newly awakened Mage has to find a cynical Etherite who can take her to the titular Tomorrowland, which is basically the Gernsback Continuum with the serial numbers filed off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-18T10:43:27-08:00","id":1168560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/401419-explain-a-movie-tv-show-comic-in-wod-terms?p=1168540#post1168540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dragon Maid doesn't really follow a pattern of &quot;Bygones avoid disbelief&quot;, as the dragons don't interfere only because the powers in their own world would become upset if they went around wreaking utter havoc. They're none the worse for wear when they use their true powers, which they often do on a normal playground, in full view of others.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well yes, obviously. Disbelief isn't a thing in that universe, so of course it wouldn't apply. No series is going to be a perfect 1:1 to World of Darkness mechanics, because the World of Darkness is chock full of its own weird idiosyncrasies.<br /> <br /> What I'M saying is that, if the 